{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"\n\n`release_on_behalf_of()` popped the waiter out of `_wait_queue` and set its event, but the woken task only added itself to `_borrowers` *after* `await event.wait()` resumed — so between the `event.set()` and the resumption (no event-loop yield in between), both guard signals in `acquire_on_behalf_of_nowait()` were false: the queue was empty and `len(_borrowers) < total_tokens`, because the woken borrower wasn't registered yet. The nowait acquire therefore saw the just-freed token as available and admitted a second borrower for it, even though the token was already logically handed to the woken waiter."}}
